  New standalone fragment: <verbatim|chapters/11-restarted-history.tex>
  (parent owns insertion/build).

  <section|Exact source packet><label|exact-source-packet>

  Martin <verbatim|restarted-rank-history.tex>:

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>211\U425 endpoint re-expression and inventory bijection;

    <item>47\U123 genuine local multipliers, scalar and regular logarithm;

    <item>145\U210 numerical short-window recurrence;

    <item>521\U743 actual adjacent-step closure and joint inflation payment;

    <item>744\Uend retained chart family and exact normalized densities.
  </itemize-minus>

  Also checked <verbatim|actual-corrected-body-compiler.tex:1\U55,130\U199>
  for recording versus budget radii and the weakened 1/48 body exponent,
  against Output Chapter 6 primitive factors/component extracted energy/joint
  tails. The argument is specific to the source construction; its ordinary
  connected-gas and logarithm estimates are cited internally to Chapter 8
  rather than reproved.

  <section|Exports><label|exports>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item><verbatim|ch11:restart-endpoint>: same original endpoint density,
    new threshold and squared radius, old path and clip coefficients, regular
    allowance retained, new forced allowance G.

    <item><verbatim|ch11:restart-family>: one retained sequence of auxiliary
    representations, one alphabet before marks, simultaneous upper/lower
    inflation bounds.

    <item><verbatim|ch11:restart-density>: exact common-coupling probability
    push, positive densities and unchanged partition function,
    coefficientwise for finite marked polynomials.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Data matching checked><label|data-matching-checked>

  Actual coupling is beta_(N,p,k), in [x_i/2,2x_i]; x_i remains the original
  adjacent clock. Recording y=r(x_i) solves fieldCut(y)=vartheta(x_i), lies
  between x_i and x_i\<twosuperior\> and is x_i^(1+o(1)). Budget radius is
  ceil(log\<twosuperior\>x_i)\<twosuperior\>, not the recording radius
  ceil(log\<twosuperior\>y). The exact radius inequalities and adjacent ratio
  are proved. The Gaussian construction retains actual path pair, forest,
  predictor derivative and clipped source with these thresholds. Holding the
  clip means its coefficients/formula, not equality of old and new threshold
  functions.

  Endpoint difference is factored before regrouping. Nonnegative direct and
  truncated-square charges pay mandatory new flag factors; all other changes
  retain true-length support weights and exact old eligibility. Components
  use full read regions, while old exclusion tests remain inside
  constituents. Every new component contains a mandatory flag factor. The
  reverse recovery of constituents establishes exact gas equality even at
  zeros of activities. Large-field selection is not replaced by independent
  flags.

  The neutral presentation deletes only the additive family for estimates.
  Genuine multipliers exp(-E_alpha)-1 remain in the actual integral and all
  marked coefficients. Its larger value bound q_n is never claimed to satisfy
  the original small derivative allowance. Owner energy pays m=G^-2, neutral
  factors pay subpower l, and joint failed-mask events are taken under the
  same actual law. The path correction is absorbed in the coarse additive
  family with its explicit sign. Hole corrections and tag multiplicities
  retain the original normalization. Positivity is deduced from kernels, not
  signed activities.

  <section|Scope and verification><label|scope-and-verification>

  The proof uses already constructed actual path/quadratic identities,
  primitive local estimates, and full-support connected expansion; it does
  not create those inputs by adding a stage request. It does construct the
  restarted representations from the original endpoint, rather than assume an
  auxiliary run exists. The separate joint Gaussian/free-detector comparison
  and all-copy OPE estimate are not claimed here.

  Static reference check found no missing labels; theorem/proof environments
  balance. No global compilation performed, as requested. Parent/UV should
  review exact use of retimed local estimates and the endpoint inventory
  bijection during integration. All thresholds are finite stage/adjacent-pair
  requests, before the physical period and marked family; no infinite-stage
  uniform constant is assumed.

  <section|Retiming correction from independent root
  review><label|retiming-correction-from-independent-root-review>

  Explicitly removed any possible invocation of the Chapter 6 coupling band
  with y=r(x): actual beta is comparable to x, not necessarily y. For each
  fixed finite estimate, beta lies in [y^(1-eta),2y] eventually. The finitely
  many inverse-coupling powers cost y^(C eta); eta is fixed sufficiently
  small before entry. The primitive exponents are correspondingly stated as
  y^(-1/4+o(1)) and weakened with strict margins to 1/24 then 1/48.
  Dimensionless gaps retain their original path bounds; physical covariance
  uses actual beta^-1. The noise ratio and positive selected energy are
  computed directly in x, giving vartheta/g comparable to h(x) and beta
  vartheta_f\<twosuperior\> bounded below by c h(x_f)\<twosuperior\>. No
  beta\<gtr\>=y/2 is used.
</body>

